  "result": "I've written the revised record for `NRS_484B_307_4b` to `record.jsonl`. It is a revision, not a withdrawal, and it hasn't been through the gate yet.\n\n**The problem:** the gate rejected the rule because nothing tied the signal head `s` to the pedestrian. The only link was \"facing\", which compares the head's position with the pedestrian's position and heading. The gate doesn't count that comparison as a tie.\n\n**The fix:** \"the highway\" in span `s4` now means the highway at the signal, linked to it through relation atoms:\n- **The junction:** the head controls an intersection `x`. Either it governs `x` directly (`dev.governs`), or it governs a lane or other travel lane `l` that runs into `x` (`st.lane_enters`).\n- **The highway:** `w` is any highway on which `x` lies (`st.highway`, `st.on_way`).\n- **The forbidden entry:** the pedestrian's footprint comes onto a roadway on `w` (`st.roadway`, `st.on_way`, `rel.occupies`), having been on no such roadway at the previous observation.\n\nThat chain runs from the head to the junction, to the highway, to the roadway, to the pedestrian, so the head is now tied to the subject.\n\n**Other changes:**\n- **Where the new atoms sit:** they are all claimed under `s4`. Spans `s1` and `s3` keep the same atoms as the earlier rules that already map these words (`NRS_484B_307_4a_o1` and `NRS_484B_307_2b`).\n- **Obligation:** it re-selects each head, junction and highway with the same conditions as the applicability. For each one, the pedestrian overlaps no roadway on that highway.\n- **Narrowing on `s4`:** it now says that a roadway of a way that doesn't meet at the signal's junction is not \"the highway\".\n- **New scenarios:**\n  - `branch_2`, expected compliant: the pedestrian steps onto a roadway of an unrelated way.\n  - `branch_3`, expected violated: the head governs the intersection itself rather than an approach lane.\n\n**Still the same:** the four exceptions, the \"facing\" test, the two proposed parameters and the four required scenarios.\n\n**Open points:**\n- **This is a reading I chose.** \"The highway\" is read as any highway that meets at the junction the signal controls. If a junction is mapped with no recorded ways (`st.on_way`), the rule will report unknown there.\n- **The sibling node `NRS_484B_307_2b`** uses the same \"facing\" test, so it will probably fail the gate the same way. That node isn't part of this repair.",
